abstract: >-
  Inspektorium is a fail-closed integrity layer for AI-generated claims and AI
  evaluation reports. Evaluators propose relations between claims and sources;
  Inspektorium checks that every claim span and quotation matches the supplied
  text exactly at its stated character offsets, keeps findings that fail a check
  out of the reportable result, and renders untrusted text so that it cannot
  forge report structure or hide warnings. Its audit workflow writes hash-bound
  bundles, records human review and releases artifacts only on an explicit step.
  Inspektorium does not judge meaning, and its scientific efficacy has not been
  established.
license: Apache-2.0
